# Line endings are decided here, not by whoever cloned the repo.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf` decides per machine. On Windows it checks out CRLF while
# git stores LF, which is self-consistent — but the same working directory opened from WSL
# is read by a second git with a different setting, and that one compares CRLF on disk
# against LF in the object store and reports every text file as modified. Nothing is
# actually different; the two gits simply disagree about what the bytes should look like.
#
# LF everywhere ends the argument. It also matches what every editor here already writes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The parser fixtures are copied out of the game and are compared byte for byte. Freezing
# them means no filter ever touches them, on any platform — the trailing spaces the game
# leaves behind survive, and so does whatever it does with line endings next patch.
#
# The parser reads both endings identically today, measured over all of them, so this is
# about the fixtures staying what was actually copied rather than about a bug.
data/sample-items/*.txt -text

# Not text. Never convert, never diff as lines.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
*.bundle binary
